  "pli-tv-kd3:5.2.6": "The Pali word translated here as “give” is <i lang='pi' translate='no'>patiṭṭhāpetu</i>, which normally means “establish”. In the present context I understand it as “establishing a gift”, in the sense that the gift is meant for the Sangha but given in the presence of the local monks. The expression <i lang='pi' translate='no'>dakkhiṇaṁ patiṭṭhāpeti</i>, “to establish a gift”, is quite common in the Suttas, see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn3.19/en/brahmali#3.2'>SN 3.19:3.2</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.61/en/brahmali#16.1'>AN 4.61:16.1</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.41/en/brahmali#5.1'>AN 5.41:5.1</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.227/en/brahmali#2.3'>AN 5.227:2.3</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an6.37/en/brahmali#1.2'>AN 6.37:1.2</a>. ",
