  "pli-tv-kd3:6.11.2": "",
  "pli-tv-kd3:6.11.3": "",
  "pli-tv-kd3:6.11.4": "The meaning of the first of these phrases, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sammā vattati</i>, is straightforward, but the last two, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>lomaṁ pāteti</i> and <i lang='pi' translate='no'>netthāraṁ vattati</i>, are more difficult. Commenting on Bu Ss 13, Sp 1.435 explains: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Na lomaṁ pātentīti anulomapaṭipadaṁ appaṭipajjanatāya na pannalomā honti. Na netthāraṁ vattantīti attano nittharaṇamaggaṁ na paṭipajjanti</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Na lomaṁ pātenti</i>: because of their non-practicing in conformity with the path, their bodily hairs are not flat. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Na netthāraṁ vattanti</i>: they are not practicing the path for their own getting out (of the offense).” My rendering attempts to capture the meaning in a non-literal way. ",
