  "pli-tv-kd3:12.1.3": "“Cowherd’s dwelling” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vaja</i>. Sp 3.203: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Vajoti gopālakānaṁ nivāsaṭṭhānaṁ</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Vajo</i> means the dwelling place of cowherds.” This is apparently a reasonably substantial dwelling with a door, as required by the commentary at Sp 3.204, and not just a sunshade as at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd3/en/brahmali#12.8.1'>Kd 3:12.8.1</a> below. ",
